1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:02,422
Big talking point was the two penalties.

2
00:00:03,563 --> 00:00:04,944
It's clear, it's clear as day.

3
00:00:05,484 --> 00:00:06,665
I don't know what more you want him to do.

4
00:00:06,725 --> 00:00:10,408
If he picked the ball up with two hands, are you going to give penalty then or not?

5
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:15,151
But I think when we try to talk to the referee, and then he just tells us to focus on

6
00:00:15,152 --> 00:00:15,452
the AFC.

7
00:00:16,492 --> 00:00:18,574
How can the referee say this? We're talking about now.

8
00:00:18,734 --> 00:00:19,715
He said, "Focus on the AFC."

9
00:00:20,675 --> 00:00:25,479
But, I mean, if you want me to go deeper, I can go deeper, but it might get me in

10
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:25,839
trouble.

11
00:00:27,032 --> 00:00:28,253
I'm a man that says it how it is.

12
00:00:28,273 --> 00:00:37,482
And yeah, I think it's clear talking points with the referee. His mind is elsewhere. The referee said this?

13
00:00:37,483 --> 00:00:40,004
The fourth referee after the match said this?

14
00:00:40,364 --> 00:00:43,427
During the checking this, he said, "Just focus on the MC," the moment we were asking him to check

15
00:00:43,567 --> 00:00:45,929
and go back to the bar and check. He said.

16
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:49,773
His earpiece is recording, so I hope he picked this up, but maybe it's switched off at that point.

17
00:00:49,774 --> 00:00:53,376
I don't know. Do you think you were wronged by the referee? It wasn't fair.

18
00:00:53,436 --> 00:00:56,218
I mean, you see this, there's two penalties.

19
00:00:56,858 --> 00:00:59,140
For me, the first one, clear penalty. Everyone sees this.

20
00:00:59,141 --> 00:01:01,762
In an unnatural position, it's a penalty.

21
00:01:01,763 --> 00:01:06,245
Throughout the season, clear penalty. But now we get to close crunch time, they change it.

22
00:01:06,246 --> 00:01:14,130
I don't know why. The last question is for the benefit of those who are wronged by the judge.

23
00:01:14,131 --> 00:01:17,412
If you said that we are wronged today, why are you angry?

24
00:01:17,413 --> 00:01:20,975
No, that's my nature, I'm excited. No, no. Okay. No, no.

25
00:01:21,055 --> 00:01:24,557
This is me, on the contrary, always like this. We know who. Who are we chasing?

26
00:01:24,558 --> 00:01:28,618
Will the other teams oppress you through the judge?

27
00:01:28,638 --> 00:01:32,440
Listen, at the end of the day, we win and we lose together.

28
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,061
And we lose gracefully.

29
00:01:35,461 --> 00:01:37,662
We don't get too low with the lows, and we don't get too high with the highs.

30
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:39,343
But we move on, we do what we can do.

31
00:01:39,443 --> 00:01:43,405
And hopefully we get some decisions and some fair ones and the right ones.

32
00:01:43,925 --> 00:01:50,468
Last question, sorry, Tony. Do you still have hope in the tournament? Of course. If we have..

33
00:01:51,756 --> 00:01:56,379
Good referees and we play how we normally play and decisions go our way.

34
00:01:56,439 --> 00:01:59,621
We have a good chance, but when it's like this, it's always going to be tough.

35
00:01:59,622 --> 00:02:01,582
but we can just concentrate on ourselves. And who knows what?

36
00:02:01,842 --> 00:02:05,865
We always meet him and we were happy with him in the family game today.

37
00:02:05,866 --> 00:02:09,407
Maybe the team was tight because he was tight. So no. I'm Blacks.

38
00:02:10,207 --> 00:02:12,669
I'm never nervous, I lose happy and I win happy.

39
00:02:12,670 --> 00:02:17,611
You know, same, same, no problem, it's within here. We love his smile.

